\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Airbnb Web Application\

\f1\b0 \
Owner: Pham Khanh Doan Tran - s3978798\
\
This project is a web application for managing Airbnb-like listings using Node.js and Express, with MongoDB as the database.\
\

\f0\b Requirements
\f1\b0 \
- Node.js (version 14.x or higher recommended)\
- MongoDB (version 3.6.0 or compatible)\
\

\f0\b Installation Instructions\

\f1\b0 1. Clone this repository to your local machine.\
2. Navigate to the project directory.\
3. Install the required dependencies: 
\f0\b npm i
\f1\b0 \
\

\f0\b Starting the Server\

\f1\b0 1. Make sure MongoDB is running on your local machine.\
2. Start the server with the following command: 
\f0\b nodemon
\f1\b0 \
3. Open your browser and navigate to 
\f0\b http://localhost:3000
\f1\b0  to access the application.\
\

\f0\b Port
\f1\b0 \
The application runs on port 3000 by default.\
\

\f0\b Dependencies\

\f1\b0 The following libraries are required and are installed via 
\f0\b npm i
\f1\b0 :\
- express - Framework for handling server requests and responses.\
- body-parser - Middleware for parsing incoming request bodies.\
- mongodb - MongoDB driver to connect to the MongoDB database.\
- nodemon - Utility that automatically restarts the server when file changes are detected.\
\

\f0\b Notes
\f1\b0 \
- Ensure MongoDB is accessible before running the application.\
- This application is currently in development mode; further enhancements and testing are ongoing.\
}